  "rules": [
    "Rounding is half away from zero on the exact binary value of the float (JavaScript's `Intl.NumberFormat(..., {roundingMode: \"halfExpand\"})` and `Number.prototype.toFixed` on |v|). Python's `round()` (half to even) is NOT used. Every rule formats |v| and puts a leading U+2212 minus sign in front when v < 0 and the formatted magnitude is not zero.",
    "Tiers are chosen on the rounded magnitude, so a value never prints as \"₹1000 crore\" or \"1.00%\".",
    "`inr` (v in ₹ crore): r0 = |v| rounded to 0 dp. r0 >= 1,00,000 -> \"₹{|v|/1e5, 2 dp} lakh crore\"; else |v| rounded to 1 dp >= 10 -> \"₹{r0 with en-IN grouping} crore\"; else \"₹{|v|, 1 dp} crore\".",
    "`pct_gdp` (v is a share of GDP, a fraction): p = 100|v|. p rounded to 1 dp >= 1 -> \"{p, 1 dp}% of GDP\"; else p rounded to 2 dp >= 0.01 -> \"{p, 2 dp}% of GDP\"; v == 0 -> \"0% of GDP\"; else \"<0.01% of GDP\".",
    "`per100` (v in ₹ per ₹100): \"₹{|v|, 1 dp}\".",
    "`pct` (v is a fraction, not of GDP): \"{100|v|, 1 dp}%\".",
    "en-IN grouping on the integer part of every number: the last three digits, then groups of two (1,23,45,678; \"₹1,234.57 lakh crore\")."
  ]
}
